' plan-122-A Phase 1, bug-484: `color.Color` is seeded into
' `resolver::BUILTIN_TYPES` PACKAGE-QUALIFIED, never as the bare leaf.
'
' A bare-leaf entry in that list makes the name resolvable from ANY file with no
' `pkg::` prefix — silently, because resolution simply succeeds. Six entries
' (`Address`, `Datagram`, `TermColor`, `TermSize`, `AudioDevice`, `Json`) once were
' bare, which is why `AS Address` compiled from a consumer while the sibling
' `AS Url` was correctly refused. This fixture is the partner assertion to
' `func_color_rgba_valid`, which proves the qualified `AS color::Color` DOES
' resolve: together they pin that exactly one of the two spellings works.

IMPORT color

FUNC main AS Integer
  LET bareLeaf AS Color = color::rgba(1, 2, 3, 4)
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
